e margins: 100px sides → content width 1240\n\nLayout plan per screen (1440 wide):\n\n**01_Home** (~5300px tall)\n- Header (100px): logo + \"Furniro\" | nav Home/Shop/About/Contact (Home current = gold/semibold) | icons\n- Hero: Photo_Hero full-bleed background (1440x716), cream card right with \"New Arrival\", \"Discover Our New Collection\", copy, BUY NOW button\n- Browse The Range: heading + sub, 3 tiles with photos Dining/Living/Bedroom\n- Our Products: heading, 8 cards grid (4 cols), Leviosa card in hover state, Show More button\n- Inspiration: \"50+ Beautiful rooms inspiration\" left, slides right with current slide overlay \"01 — Bed Room / Inner Peace\" + arrow, next chevron, dots (4, current 1)\n- Share your setup: \"Share your setup with\" / \"#FurniroFurniture\" + 9 photos collage\n- Footer\n\n**02_Shop** (~3400px)\n- Header (Shop current)\n- Page banner: Photo_Page_Banner, \"Shop\", breadcrumb Home › Shop\n- Toolbar: Filter, grid, list | Showing 1–16 of 32 results | Show 16 | Sort by Default\n- Products: 16 cards (8×2), first Leviosa hover\n- Pagination: 1 2 3 Next (1 current)\n- Features strip\n- Footer\n\n**03_Product** (~3500px)\n- Breadcrumb bar: Home › Shop › Asgaard sofa\n- Gallery left (main + 4 thumbnails), summary right: title, price, rating 4.7 stars + 204 Customer Reviews, short desc, Size L/XL/XS (L selected), Color purple/black/gold, quantity stepper −1+, Add To Cart, + Compare, SKU/Category/Tags, Share social logos\n- Description tabs: Description | Additional Information | Reviews [204], current Description, 2 paragraphs, 2 cloud sofa photos\n- Related Products: Syltherine, Leviosa, Lolito, Respira cards + Show More\n- Footer\n\n**04_Cart_Drawer**: 03_Product page as backdrop (dimmed/inactive) + drawer right: \"Shopping Cart\", close icon, item Asgaard sofa × 1 Rs. 250,000.00, remove icon, Subtotal, Cart/Checkout/Comparison buttons\n\n**05_Comparison** (~2800px)\n- Header (no current), banner \"Product Comparison\", breadcrumb Home › Comparison\n- Intro: \"Go to Product page for more Products\" + View More | two product cards (Asgaard Sofa, Outdoor Sofa Set with photo, price, rating, reviews) | Add A Product + Choose a Product dropdown\n- Specifications: General, Product, Dimensions, Warranty groups, two value columns + Add To Cart under each\n- Features strip, Footer\n\n**06_Cart** (~2000px)\n- Header, banner \"Cart\", breadcrumb\n- Cart table: Product | Price | Quantity | Subtotal, row Asgaard sofa with remove\n- Cart Totals card: Subtotal, Total, Check Out\n- Features strip, Footer\n\n**07_Checkout** (~2400px)\n- Header, banner \"Checkout\", breadcrumb\n- Billing details form: First Name, Last Name, Company Name (Optional), Country/Region Sri Lanka, Street address, Town/City, Province Western Province, ZIP code, Phone, Email address, Additional information\n- Order summary: Product/Subtotal rows, Asgaard sofa × 1, totals, payment radio Direct Bank Transfer (selected, with note) / Cash On Delivery, privacy note, Place order\n- Features strip, Footer\n\n**08_Contact** (~2200px)\n- Header (Contact current), banner \"Contact\", breadcrumb\n- Intro: \"Get In Touch With Us\" + copy\n- Left: Address/Phone/Working Time with icons; Right: form (Your name, Email address, Subject, Message, Submit)\n- Features strip, Footer\n\n**09_Blog** (~3000px)\n- Header, banner \"Blog\", breadcrumb\n- Posts: 3 large post cards with photo, meta (Admin/14 Oct 2022/category), title, excerpt, Read more\n- Sidebar: search, Categories with counts, Recent Posts with thumbs\n- Pagination 1 2 3 Next\n- Features strip, Footer\n\nPrototype links:\n- 01: Shop nav → 02; BUY NOW → 02; Show More → 02; any product card → 03; Compare (hover) → 05; cart → 06; Contact nav → 08\n- 02: product card → 03; Compare → 05; Home → 01; cart → 06\n- 03: Add To Cart → 04; + Compare → 05; Shop breadcrumb → 02; related cards → 03\n- 04: Cart → 06; Checkout → 07; Comparison → 05; close → 03\n- 05: View More → 02; Add To Cart → 06\n- 06: Check Out → 07; Asgaard sofa → 03\n- 07: Place order → entry only (no link)\n- 08: Home → 01\n- 09: Home → 01\n\nAlso footer links can link to Blog (09_Blog link from footer).\n\nApproach: I'll build components first (Header, Footer, ProductCard, ProductCardHover, FeaturesStrip, PageBanner, Button etc. — actually the given Button component exists; I can use it or make my own variants). Given the complexity, I'll write helper JS functions in use_figma to build efficiently.\n\nStrategy: Build a shared components section in the workspace page, then build each frame using instances. To keep things manageable, I'll write code with helper functions and run in sections:\n\n1. Setup: load fonts, get workspace page, create color palette frame + core components (Header, Footer, ProductCard, ProductCardHover, FeatureStrip, PageBanner)\n2. Build 01_Home\n3. Build 02_Shop\n4. Build 03_Product\n5. Build 04_Cart_Drawer\n6. Build 05_Comparison\n7. Build 06_Cart\n8. Build 07_Checkout\n9. Build 08_Contact\n10. Build 09_Blog\n11. Wire prototype\n12. Screenshot & verify\n\nLet me think about the code structure. Each use_figma call runs in isolation, so I need to re-define helpers each time or write compact code. I'll write a compact helper set per call.\n\nFor images: the media items are COMPONENTS (symbols). I create instances with figma.getNodeByIdAsync('13:9').createInstance(). Instances of photo components can be resized; the component likely has an image fill. I should check one to understand structure. Let me inspect Photo_Hero component (13:9) to see its fills and whether resize works. Instances can't be cropped internally easily, but I can place them inside clipping frames (clipsContent) to crop. That's the standard approach.\n\nAlso note: component instances resizing — a photo component instance can be resized if constraints allow. Simpler: put instance in a frame with clipsContent=true and scale. Actually instances can be resized directly via resize() — contents scale? No, contents follow constraints. If the photo component's child uses left-right/top-bottom constraints or scale, resize works. Let me check the structure of one photo component first.\n\nLet me first check workspace page content and inspect a couple of components.\n\nPlan for the helper approach: since each call is separate, I'll define a `C` object with colors and helper functions in each call. Keep code compact but readable.\n\nFonts: Poppins Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold, plus maybe Light/ExtraLight for big display? Keep to Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold. Need figma.loadFontAsync for each used style before setting characters.\n\nFont names in Figma: family \"Poppins\", styles: \"Regular\", \"Medium\", \"Semi Bold\", \"Bold\", \"Italic\" etc.\n\nLet me start. First inspect workspace and one photo component + Button + TextField structure.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4169e7d1-fa58-4180-9c80-2a57d8444911","uuid":"ca17eecc-04aa-4e4f-b30f-6cbb2c3cc0fd","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:14:02.066Z","thinking_duration_ms":40787}
