{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":37885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"021f6ae78f840a7a46b06fd34c924a30","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The workspace is empty. The photos are image-filled components. Button is a gold component with white text, 222x74. Text Field is 453x111 with label and input frame.\n\nNow let me check fonts loaded in Button and Text Field (what fonts they use). Let me also check the font of the Button text and Text Field.\n\nLet me check fonts, then plan the build. I'll need to:\n1. Load fonts: Poppins in various weights (Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold), Montserrat maybe for \"Furniro\" wordmark (in the original Furniro it's Montserrat). But brief says \"Use Poppins for all UI text\". So Poppins for everything. Let me load Poppins variants.\n\nPlan of the design system:\n- Brand gold #B88E2F\n- Neutrals: text #1A1A1F / #333, gray #9F9F9F, light gray backgrounds #F9F1E7 (original Furniro tint) — actually the original kit uses #FFF3E3 hero card, #F9F1E7 features strip, #FAF3EA toolbar. I'll define: background #FFFFFF, surface tint #FAF3EA (warm cream), features strip #FAF3EA, badge sale red #E97171, badge new green #2EC1AC, rating yellow stars (media default).\n\nBuild order:\n1. Create design tokens (not variables necessarily — just use colors consistently).\n2. Create components in the workspace page: first a \"Library\" area at top of workspace? Actually, workspace page will hold the 9 frames. Components can be created anywhere; let me create them on the workspace page in a separate section off to the side (x = -1600 or below the frames). Reusable components required: Header, Footer, ProductCard (+ hover variant state via separate component or boolean), PageTitle (banner + breadcrumb), FeatureStrip, Pagination, Button variants (reuse given Button for primary), Badge, Tabs, Quantity stepper, Size/Color picker, CartDrawer, etc.\n\nGiven the constraints of building via plugin API, I should build components as needed and instance them across frames. Key reusable ones: Header (with current-state overrides — I can make one Header component with a text override for current; simpler: build header directly per frame? But \"Component reuse\" is evaluated. Let me make Header a component with instance swapping for current nav item — simpler: create Header component with nav texts, and for \"current\" styling use per-instance overrides on the text color/weight. Instances allow text/fill overrides on children. So one Header component; per instance, override the current nav text (gold + semibold).\n\nFooter: one component, instanced on all 9 frames.\n\nProductCard: component with photo area, badge slot, name, desc, price, old price. Two variants: default and hover. I could use a component with a boolean property \"hover\" (Figma supports component properties, but toggling hidden overlay via boolean property is doable). Simpler: two separate components? Better: one component set with variants \"state=default/hover\"? Creating variant sets via API is possible (figma.combineAsVariants). That may be overkill; a cleaner approach: create \"ProductCard\" component (default). Create a second component \"ProductCard / Hover\" that includes the overlay. Instances allow overriding images (fills) and texts, so a single ProductCard component can be instanced 16 times with different photos and names via fill overrides (instance overrides of fills allowed? Yes, fill overrides on nested nodes within instances are allowed as long as the node structure matches).\n\nFor photos: The media are components with IMAGE fills. To place a photo in my design: instance the photo component, resize to fit (scaleMode FILL keeps crop fill when resized? The image fill has scaleMode FILL so resizing the instance crops accordingly — good).\n\nApproach for ProductCard: within my component, include an instance of a Photo component and swap via instanceSwap... but all photo components are in the reference file — swapping requires them to be in same document — they are (same file, different page). componentNode.createInstance() works with any component in the same document. Instance swap: instance.swapComponent(otherComponent). That works across pages in same document. \n\nSo ProductCard component has a photo instance (e.g. Photo_Product_Syltherine); for other products, swapComponent to the respective photo. Overriding text in instances is fine.\n\nSimilarly Header contains instances of Icon components; Footer has Logo; etc.\n\nPhoto components: since fills are images inside the component root itself (fills on the component node), resizing the instance works. Crop freely = resize.\n\nLet me now check the font used in Button text (probably Poppins). Then set up.\n\nAlso check whether Poppins fonts are available. I'll load: Poppins Regular, Medium, SemiBold (\"Semi Bold\"? For Poppins in Figma, the style names are \"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\",\"Light\",\"ExtraBold\"? Actually Figma's Poppins styles: \"Thin\",\"ExtraLight\",\"Light\",\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\",\"ExtraBold\",\"Black\" and italics. Hmm — for \"Inter\" it's \"Semi Bold\" but for Poppins it's \"SemiBold\" (no space) because Poppins uses that naming. The gotcha note says specifically for Inter. Let me test loading and see which works.\n\nLet me also verify the Button component's text font to match style naming.\n\nNext step: call use_figma to check fonts of button text, and list available Poppins font styles? The plugin API can't list fonts, but figma.loadFontAsync throws if unavailable. I'll attempt loads with try/catch for candidates.\n\nThen build the design system helpers. Because code is limited to 50000 chars per call, I'll break work into many calls:\n\nCall A: setup — create page structure helpers, colors, font loading, create a \"· Components\" area at bottom of workspace; create base components: Badge, Button variants? Let me carefully plan the components:\n\nComponents to build (in workspace, at y offset below frames, e.g. y=20000 area, or x=-2500):\n\n1. `Furniro / Header` — 1440 wide, logo instance + \"Furniro\" wordmark, nav links (Home Shop About Contact), icons row (account, search, heart, cart).\n2. `Furniro / Footer` — 1440 wide footer with brand, address, Links, Help, Newsletter, divider, copyright.\n3. `Furniro / ProductCard` — default state.\n4. `Furniro / ProductCardHover` — hover state (or variant).\n5. `Furniro / Badge` — sale (red) & new (green) as separate? One component with color override per instance; simple.\n6. `Furniro / PageTitle` — banner bg + title + breadcrumb (breadcrumb text override per page).\n7. `Furniro / FeatureStrip` — the 4 features row.\n8. `Furniro / Pagination` — pages 1 2 3 Next.\n9. `Furniro / PrimaryButton` — the given Button instance? The given Button is 222x74 gold with white text \"Button\" — I can instance it and override text (\"BUY NOW\", \"Show More\", \"Explore More\", \"SUBSCRIBE\", \"Place order\", \"Check Out\", \"Add To Cart\", \"Submit\", \"View More\"...). Actually the original kit has varied button styles (outline, text). I can reuse the given Button component for primary gold buttons and define secondary styles as separate components (e.g. outline button for \"Add To Cart\" on product page — in the original kit, \"Add To Cart\" is an outlined button, \"+ Compare\" is dark). To honor \"reuse the given components\", I'll use the given Button for gold CTAs and the given Text Field for form inputs.\n\nFor flexibility with button sizes: overriding width of instance is allowed (resize instance). Text auto layout? The given Button component — does it have auto layout? Unknown. If not, resizing won't center text. Let me check its layout mode in the next inspection. If no autolayout, I'll create my own Button component (gold) and still instance the given one somewhere? The brief says \"Default Button, default Text Field\" are given — \"reuse the components in 02·Components\". Best to actually reuse them. I can check layoutMode; if none, I could wrap: create instance, then it's fixed; resizing instance distorts. Alternative: detach? No — reuse means use as instances. Hmm. Let me check its constraints/layout first. Actually for evaluation \"Component reuse\" refers to building own components as reusable. Using given Button is item \"Fixed (given)\" — media and default button/textfield. I'll try to instance them where possible, but if resizing is a problem, I'll build my own button component matching the given style (gold #B88E2F, white text, radius) and also use given Button where size fits. Let me inspect the Button's layoutMode and cornerRadius.\n\nAlso Text Field 453x75 input with label — check layout.\n\nLet me also decide on whether to use auto layout extensively. Building with auto layout makes precise, clean design. But instance overrides + autolayout can be finicky. I'll use a hybrid: absolute positioning with computed coordinates in code (deterministic), and auto layout for repetitive rows (features strip, footer columns, pagination). Given evaluation is visual, absolute positioning with exact coordinates is safest.\n\nTime/token budget: 15M tokens is plenty. The main risk is code size per call and errors. I'll write a small helper library (createText, createFrame, place instance) at the start of each call (self-contained).\n\nStructure plan per frame (1440 wide):\n\n**01_Home** (height ~6100)\n- Header (h~100)\n- Hero: Photo_Hero full-width 1440x~780 crop, card #FFF3E3 on right with New Arrival / Discover Our New Collection / sub / BUY NOW (gold button)\n- Browse The Range: title + sub, 3 tiles with photos + labels\n- Our Products: title, 8 cards grid 4x2 (285 wide each, card ~285x446), Show More button (outline gold)\n- Inspiration section: dark? Original: cream bg with carousel. Left text (title, sub, Explore More gold button), right slides: main slide (Photo_Inspiration_Inner_Peace) with card overlay \"01 — Bed Room / Inner Peace / arrow button\", plus slide 2, 3 peeking, chevron next button, dots indicator (4, current 1)\n- Share your setup: title lines + collage of 9 setup photos\n- Footer\n\n**02_Shop** (~2500)\n- Header (current Shop)\n- PageTitle \"Shop\" + breadcrumb\n- Toolbar (cream bg): filter icon + \"Filter\", grid/list icons, divider, \"Showing 1–16 of 32 results\"; right: \"Show\" [16 box] \"Sort by\" [Default box + chevron]\n- 16 product cards (4x4), first Leviosa card hover state — wait: \"the 8 products of DATA, then the same 8 again; the first Leviosa card is in its hover state\". So Leviosa (2nd card of first row) hover.\n- Pagination row centered\n- FeatureStrip\n- Footer\n\n**03_Product** (~3300)\n- Header (current Shop)\n- Breadcrumb bar (cream) Home › Shop › Asgaard sofa\n- Product section: left gallery (main 423x500 Photo_Asgaard_Sofa on cream bg + 4 thumbs row), right: title \"Asgaard sofa\", price, rating stars + divider + \"204 Customer Reviews\", short desc, Size (L XL XS selected L), Color (3 dots), quantity stepper + Add To Cart (outline) + \"+ Compare\" (dark), meta SKU/Category/Tags/Share with social logos\n- Description tabs: tabs centered (Description, Additional Information, Reviews [204]), text 2 paragraphs, 2 cloud sofa photos side by side\n- Related Products: title, 4 cards (Syltherine, Leviosa, Lolito, Respira), Show More\n- Footer\n\n**04_Cart_Drawer** (~ same height as product page top portion — frame shows product page dimmed + drawer). Frame height: make it equal to 03_Product? The drawer overlays top of product page. Simplest: copy of 03_Product content dimmed behind (opacity overlay) + right drawer 417 wide with Shopping Cart title, close icon, divider, item (photo + name + 1 × price + remove), Subtotal, three buttons Cart / Checkout / Comparison. Frame height can be shorter (e.g. 1300) — \"Behind the drawer: the 03_Product page, inactive\". I'll make 04_Cart_Drawer same as 03_Product frame but with dark overlay + drawer. To keep manageable, height maybe ~1500 showing top of product page. Hmm — checklist evaluation: must include behind=03_Product page inactive + drawer contents. A partial product page behind (top part) is fine since it says \"the 03_Product page\". Safer: full duplicate of 03_Product, dimmed. That's a lot of nodes but I can duplicate the finished 03_Product frame? Frames can't contain frames as... they can. Approach: build 04 by cloning 03 frame, add overlay rect + drawer. Cloning via frame.clone() — but 03 contains instances; clone preserves. Then change frame name to 04_Cart_Drawer, resize? Keep same size. Add overlay + drawer. Then add prototype links on the drawer. \n\n**05_Comparison** (~2600)\n- Header (no current)\n- PageTitle \"Product Comparison\", breadcrumb Home › Comparison\n- Row: \"Go to Product page for more Products\" + \"View More\" | product card A (Asgaard: photo, name, price, rating) | product B (Outdoor Sofa Set) | \"Add A Product\" + \"Choose a Product\" gold select\n- Specifications table: groups General / Product / Dimensions / Warranty; rows: label + value A + value B (3 columns). Under each product \"Add To Cart\" — \"one value per product on every row (see DATA) · 'Add To Cart' under each product\" — the Add To Cart buttons appear in the table under each product column (in original kit, after specs, buttons row). I'll place two gold \"Add To Cart\" buttons under each product column at the end of Warranty group.\n- FeatureStrip, Footer\n\n**06_Cart** (~1500)\n- Header (no current)\n- PageTitle \"Cart\" + breadcrumb\n- Left: cart table (header row cream bg: Product Price Quantity Subtotal; row: photo, Asgaard sofa, price, qty box 1, subtotal, delete icon)\n- Right: Cart Totals card (cream): Subtotal, Total (gold), \"Check Out\" outline button\n- FeatureStrip, Footer\n\n**07_Checkout** (~2100)\n- Header (none current)\n- PageTitle \"Checkout\"\n- Left: \"Billing details\" title, form fields: First Name / Last Name (side by side), Company Name (Optional), Country/Region select (Sri Lanka + chevron), Street address, Town/City, Province select, ZIP code, Phone, Email address, Additional information — use Text Field component instances with label overrides.\n- Right: order summary: rows Product/Subtotal headers, Asgaard sofa × 1 / Rs. 250,000.00, Subtotal, Total (gold large). Payment radios: Direct Bank Transfer (selected, with note text), Cash On Delivery. Privacy note with \"privacy policy\" link styled. \"Place order\" outline button.\n- FeatureStrip, Footer\n\n**08_Contact** (~2100)\n- Header (current Contact)\n- PageTitle \"Contact\"\n- Intro: \"Get In Touch With Us\" + copy, centered\n- Left column: Address/Phone/Working Time with icons + text\n- Right: form Your name, Email address, Subject, Message (textarea), Submit gold button\n- FeatureStrip, Footer\n\n**09_Blog** (~2700)\n- Header (none current)\n- PageTitle \"Blog\"\n- Left: 3 post cards (photo, meta row icons: Admin, 14 Oct 2022, category; title; excerpt; Read more)\n- Right sidebar: search field (search icon), Categories list with counts, Recent Posts (5 items with thumbnails)\n- Pagination 1 2 3 Next\n- FeatureStrip, Footer\n\nPrototype links (per brief):\n01: Shop nav → 02; BUY NOW → 02; Show More → 02; product cards → 03; Compare (hover Leviosa) → 05; cart icon → 06; Contact nav → 08. Also maybe footer blog link → 09 (add \"Blog\" link? Footer Links fixed: Home Shop About Contact. Brief says link blog \"from wherever you see fit (e.g. the footer)\". I could add a small \"Blog\" link in footer? Footer Links fixed data says Home·Shop·About·Contact. Hmm, adding Blog might violate \"Copy and data must match Fixed data exactly\". Better: add blog link elsewhere — e.g., in 01 home footer? Or link from nav? Nav is fixed too. Option: make \"Read more\" on 09 posts entry-only. For entry to 09: \"the source has no entry point to the blog — link it from wherever you see fit (e.g. the footer)\". Adding \"Blog\" under Help column? That changes copy. Alternatively on 01_Home's footer logo area? Simplest compliant approach: add a \"Blog\" link in footer Help/Links... risky. Alternative: link from 08_Contact intro? Hmm. I think adding \"Blog\" as a fifth footer link is acceptable given explicit brief suggestion \"e.g. the footer\". Fixed data lists Links: Home·Shop·About·Contact — adding Blog technically deviates. But the brief explicitly invites adding a blog entry point wherever fit. I'll add \"Blog\" to the footer Links column (keeps all fixed entries, adds one). That satisfies both reasonably. Also 09_Blog links back Home.\n\n02: product card → 03; Compare (hover) → 05; Home nav/breadcrumb → 01; cart → 06.\n03: Add To Cart → 04 (overlay/navigate); + Compare → 05; Shop breadcrumb → 02; related cards → 03 (self).\n04: Cart → 06; Checkout → 07; Comparison → 05; close → 03.\n05: View More → 02; Add To Cart → 06.\n06: Check Out → 07; Asgaard sofa → 03.\n07: Place order → entry only (no frame) — so no link needed. \n08: Home nav/breadcrumb → 01.\n09: Home → 01.\n\nAlso header cart icon on all frames → 06. Nav Home → 01, Shop → 02, Contact → 08 on all frames. I'll add these on Header instances: reactions can't be added to instances inside a component... Prototype interactions on nested elements within instances: you CAN add reactions to nodes inside an instance? In Figma UI you can add interactions to elements inside instances. Via API: reactions property is settable on nodes within instances? I believe instance children overrides for reactions are supported in the API (reactions are an overridable property). Let me test — safer: set reactions on the Header component itself (nav Home → 01 etc.) since those links are identical on all frames. Reactions set on the main component propagate to instances! Yes — prototype interactions defined on the component main carry into instances. But careful: on frame 04 (clone of 03) links remain fine.\n\nHowever destination frames must exist when setting reactions. So prototype wiring comes last, after frames exist.\n\nPlan components to build first (in workspace, in a \"Components\" section frame at x=-2000 area or below). I'll put a vertical section starting at y=0 but at x=-1800? Frame coordinates: workspace page empty; I'll place screens at x=0.. with spacing: rows of frames. Actually simpler: arrange 9 frames in a grid 2 columns? Common: stack vertically or grid. I'll do grid: 3 columns x spacing 160, frames width 1440 each → columns at x=0, 1600, 3200; rows heights vary. Or single column for easy prototype navigation? Prototype flows work regardless of position. I'll do 3 columns × 3 rows: row1: 01,02,03; row2: 04,05,06; row3: 07,08,09. Row heights: need each frame's height to compute row y. I'll set explicit heights when building each. Row1 max ≈ 6100 (01). That's a huge gap under 02/03. Alternative: column-major: col1: 01 (tall), 04; col2: 02, 05, 07; col3: 03, 06, 08, 09. Eh. Simplest: single column, x=0, y accumulating with 240 gap. Height total ~ 6100+2500+3300+3300(04 same as 03)+2600+1500+2100+2100+2700 ≈ 26200. Figma canvas fine. Components section at x = -2200.\n\nHmm, but for screenshots and review a single column is fine.\n\nLet me define exact layout numbers per frame as I build.\n\nFirst, gather more details: check Button layout mode, corner radius; Text Field layout; check Logo_Furniro size (72x72); check a few icons; check available Poppins styles by attempting loads. Also inspect the given Button text font family.\n\nLet me also figure out `reactions` API: node.reactions = [{action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', ...}, trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}]. I'll use that.\n\nOverlay for 04: the brief wants a frame showing product page + drawer; using NAVIGATE to 04_Cart_Drawer frame is acceptable (\"Add To Cart opens 04_Cart_Drawer over the product page\" — they made it a frame, one state per frame, wire as clickable prototype; so NAVIGATE to frame 04 is right).\n\nOK next call: inspect Button cornerRadius/layoutMode, Text Field details, and test Poppins font loading with a probe node.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4169e7d1-fa58-4180-9c80-2a57d8444911","uuid":"fc439672-0a56-4297-bea3-920ae9dde805","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:15:52.353Z","thinking_duration_ms":96371}
