{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":38606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"04036ae78ff40a7a6ce54e8c143cc117","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All fonts available. Button: gold fill, Poppins Medium 16 white text, 222x74 auto layout. Text Field: vertical AL, label Poppins Medium 16, input white with #9F9F9F stroke, radius 10, 453x75, placeholder Regular 16.\n\nNow build step 1: core builder library + Header + Footer components. I'll place components on the workspace page at x = -2000 (off to the left) so they don't interfere with screens starting at x=0.\n\nLet me write the first big call. Include:\n- C constants\n- hex()\n- loadFonts\n- makeTxt (with async font loading per call)\n- helpers: rect, autolayout config\n- asset component cache by id; place(id) → instance\n- icon(id, size)\n- Header builder (component), Footer builder (component)\n\nComponent placement on workspace page: y=0, x=-2500 for a components \"area\". Figma components can't be inside a section easily; I'll just place them on the page. Name components with \"F/\" prefix.\n\nHeader component: width 1440, height 100, white bg, horizontal AL, padding [0,100], spacing 0. Inner: logo row (logo 50? media logo is 72 tall — resize to 40x40ish; Logo_Furniro is square 72 → resize 48x48), \"Furniro\" text 34 bold black; spacer; nav row spacing 75: Home/Shop/About/Contact (16 medium black; current → gold #B88E2F + semibold); spacer; icon row spacing 45: account 28, search 28, heart 28, cart 28.\n\nUse auto layout with spacingBetween? In auto layout, use itemSpacing for uniform, but we need groups. Structure: Header (H-AL, padding 100 L/R, fill white, height 100):\n - Frame \"Left\" (H-AL, gap 8): logo instance 48, \"Furniro\" text 34 Bold, color #000. vertically centered.\n - Frame \"Nav\" (H-AL, gap 75): 4 nav texts.\n - Frame \"Actions\" (H-AL, gap 45): 4 icons.\nTo distribute: make three children and set nav/actions spacing via a layout trick: set Header layoutAlign? In H-AL with three children, use \"space-between\": Figma supports itemSpacing... there's `layoutMode` + primaryAxisAlignItems = 'SPACE_BETWEEN'. Yes! primaryAxisAlignItems 'SPACE_BETWEEN' works when there's more than 2 children? Yes, space-between works with any count in Figma.\n\nSo Header: primaryAxisSizingMode 'FIXED' height 100? For component height fixed 100, width fixed 1440. counterAxisAlignItems 'CENTER'.\n\nFor instances of Header with different current nav: use text overrides + color overrides per instance in screens. The current item styling: color gold + weight semibold. Overrides on text nodes inside instances are allowed.\n\nFooter component: width 1440, white bg, top area padding 48 top? Structure: V-AL padding [48,100,38,100], gap 0. Contains:\n - Divider line top? In original, footer has a horizontal divider between content and bottom row, and content bottom border. Structure:\n   - \"FooterMain\" H-AL, width fill, primaryAxis SPACE_BETWEEN, padding bottom 48: \n     - Col1 V-AL gap 50: \"Furniro.\" 24 Bold; address text 16 regular #9F9F9F width 285.\n     - Col2 V-AL gap 55 (label) / 46 items: \"Links\" 16 medium #9F9F9F; Home, Shop, About, Contact 16 medium black.\n     - Col3: \"Help\"; Payment Options, Returns, Privacy Policies.\n     - Col4: \"Newsletter\"; row: input underlined \"Enter Your Email Address\" (14 regular #9F9F9F with bottom border via a 1px line rect) + \"SUBSCRIBE\" 14 medium with underline (border-bottom). I'll implement underline as 1px rect under text. To keep simpler: V-AL; row frame H-AL gap 11: (V-AL gap 4: text + line 200x1) + (V-AL gap 4: text SUBSCRIBE + line 77x1).\n   - Divider line 1440-wide (fill width) 1px #D9D9D9.\n   - Bottom text \"2023 Furniro. All rights reserved\" 16 regular, padding top 35.\n\nUse actual V-AL with items: Footer: V-AL padding [48,0,38,0]; child FooterMain (H-AL fill width, padding [0,100,48,100], SPACE_BETWEEN), divider (rect height 1, fill HORIZONTAL, color #D9D9D9, layoutAlign STRETCH), bottom frame (H-AL fill width padding [35,100,0,100]) with text.\n\nFor col2 \"About\" link → entry-only. Footer links are entry points? \"→ Shop (nav)\" etc. Footer \"Shop\" links are entry-only too? The links listed per frame only mention nav and breadcrumb. So footer links no reactions. But 09_Blog entry: \"link it from wherever you see fit (e.g. the footer)\". So I'll add a \"Blog\" link? Footer Links column data is fixed: Home · Shop · About · Contact only. Hmm — \"Footer: see DATA (Footer)\" is fixed; adding Blog to links would violate fixed data? It says Links: Home · Shop · About · Contact. I could add a small \"Blog\" link elsewhere — e.g., in header nav? Header nav fixed too (Home/Shop/About/Contact). Alternative: add blog entry from footer Copyright? Hmm. Or add a \"Read our blog →\" link somewhere on Home (e.g., in Share your setup section?). The brief: \"09_Blog: the source has no entry point to the blog — link it from wherever you see fit (e.g. the footer).\" So I'll add a \"Blog\" link in the footer's Help column? Help: Payment Options · Returns · Privacy Policies fixed. I could add an extra \"Blog\" line at the bottom of the Links column — it's an addition, not changing existing copy. I'll add \"Blog\" as a 5th item in the Links column, styled like others, with a prototype link to 09_Blog. Reasonable.\n\nActually wait — reactions on a component instance... if I add the reaction to the \"Blog\" text inside the Footer component itself, then every footer instance links to 09_Blog. Good — add it once in the component.\n\nSimilarly header nav Home/Shop/Contact reactions can be added inside Header component → all instances get links. Header is a component with current states per instance; nav text overrides don't affect reactions. Cart icon in header → 06_Cart. Add reactions in component: Home→01, Shop→02, Contact→08, cart→06. That covers every page automatically. \n\nNow the components page position: put components at x=-3000, stacked vertically with labels. Actually simplest: each component placed on page at y positions accumulating. Components directly on page canvas.\n\nLet me define the full color palette:\n- C.gold = B88E2F\n- C.goldDark = 96742C? for pressed? not needed.\n- C.ink = 000000 (headings) — maybe 3A3A3A? Use pure black for headings per original.\n- C.text = 3A3A3A (product names)\n- C.muted = 9F9F9F\n- C.soft = 666666 (secondary body)\n- C.cream = FCF8F3\n- C.light = F4F5F7 (card info bg)\n- C.banner = F9F1E7 (toolbar bg)\n- C.border = D9D9D9\n- C.line = E8E8E8? use D9D9D9 consistently. Also EAEAEA for table borders. I'll add C.line = EAEAEA.\n- C.white, C.dark = 262626, C.red = E97171, C.green = 2EC1AC, C.yellow = FFC700.\n\nType scale (Poppins):\n- h1: 48 Bold (page titles, hero heading... hero \"Discover Our New Collection\" 52 Bold gold) — I'll use 52 for hero.\n- h2: 40 Bold (section titles)\n- h3: 36 Medium (Get In Touch, Billing details → 36 semibold)\n- h4: 32 SemiBold (footer \"Furniro.\" 24)\n- title24: 24 SemiBold\n- body: 16 Regular\n- bodyMedium: 16 Medium\n- small: 14 Regular / 14 Medium\n- tiny: 13 Regular\n\nEffects: \n- E.cardShadow: drop shadow 0 8 24 rgba(0,0,0,0.08) — for drawer stronger: -8? Drawer: shadow X -16? Drawer sits right; shadow to left: {x:-16,y:0,blur:40,color rgba(0,0,0,0.12)}.\n- Elevation for overlay cards subtle.\n\nRadii: r.sm 4, r.md 8, r.lg 10, r.xl 16, r.pill 999.\n\nNow write call 1: setup + Header + Footer + IconRow helpers. Also helper to add prototype reactions inside components.\n\nPrototype reaction API: node.reactions = [{action:{type:'NODE', destinationId: id, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null}, trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}}]. For overlays: action type 'NODE', navigation: 'OVERLAY', transition..., overlayRelativePosition etc. For close overlay: navigation:'CLOSE', or action type 'CLOSE'? For closing: {trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'CLOSE_TOP_OVERLAY'}}? Actually in plugin API: reaction action {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE'}; for close: {type:'CLOSE_TOP_OVERLAY'}? Hmm. The modern API: reactions: [{trigger, action}] where action = {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE'|'OVERLAY'|'SWAP'|'SCROLL_TO', transition, overlaySettings...} or {type:'BACK'}, {type:'CLOSE'}? Let me recall: `navigation` enum: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"OVERLAY\" | \"SWAP\" | \"SCROLL_TO\" | \"CHANGE_TO\". For close overlay action, action type is 'CLOSE_TOP_OVERLAY'? Hmm... Actually I believe: Reaction = {trigger: Trigger, action: Action}; Action = {type: 'NODE', destinationId, navigation, ...} | {type: 'BACK'} | {type: 'CLOSE' } | {type: 'URL', url}. The close action type is 'CLOSE'. Let me be careful: Plugin API docs: Action type: \"BACK\" | \"CLOSE\" | \"URL\" | \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\" | \"NODE\". Yes 'CLOSE' exists (closes top overlay). \n\nFor overlay open: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'OVERLAY', transition:{type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'RIGHT', duration:0.3, easing:'EASE_OUT'}, overlaySettings:{position:'MANUAL' or relativePosition...}}? Simplify: since 04_Cart_Drawer is itself a full-screen frame (1440 wide including dim+drawer), using NAVIGATE to it is simplest and satisfies \"Add To Cart → 04_Cart_Drawer\". The brief says drawer frame shows product page behind inactive — so it's a full-screen frame. So all links are NAVIGATE. \n\nI'll implement reaction helper: link(node, destId) sets node.reactions. Must be careful: reactions can only be set on nodes in... any node. And destination must be a top-level frame? NAVIGATE destination must be a frame in same page. Our screens are top-level frames on workspace. Good.\n\nTiming: add reactions at the end when all screens exist (destination ids must exist — actually you can set destinationId to any node id that exists at time of setting). I'll add all reactions in a final call. But for header/footer components, reactions set inside components once.\n\nWait: does NAVIGATE from a component instance inside a frame work in prototype? Yes — reactions inside components work (like links in repeated elements).\n\nOK, code call 1. I must keep code under 50000 chars. Header+Footer+helpers ~ manageable.\n\nAlso create \"F/IconButton\"? Not needed separately.\n\nLet me define helper functions in code:\n\n```js\nconst WS = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('15:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(WS);\nconst C = {...};\nconst hex = h => { const n=parseInt(h,16); return {r:((n>>16)&255)/255, g:((n>>8)&255)/255, b:(n&255)/255}; };\nconst F = {reg:{family:'Poppins',style:'Regular'}, med:..., sb:..., bold:..., light:...};\nasync function txt(str, size, font, colorHex, opts={}){ const t=figma.createText(); await figma.loadFontAsync(font); t.fontName=font; t.fontSize=size; t.characters=str; t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:hex(colorHex)}]; if(opts.lh) t.lineHeight={unit:'PERCENT',value:opts.lh}; if(opts.w){t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(opts.w, t.height);} if(opts.ls) t.letterSpacing={unit:'PERCENT',value:opts.ls}; if(opts.align) t.textAlignHorizontal=opts.align; return t; }\n```\n\nNote: textAutoResize HEIGHT with fixed width: resize after setting textAutoResize='HEIGHT' then t.resize(w, h) — h auto? For textAutoResize 'HEIGHT', width fixed, height auto. Set t.resize(w, t.height) works.\n\nAL helper:\n```js\nfunction al(node, {mode='VERTICAL', gap=0, pad=[0,0,0,0], wrap=false, main='MIN', cross='MIN', mainSize='AUTO', crossSize='AUTO'}={}) { node.layoutMode=mode; node.itemSpacing=gap; node.paddingTop=pad[0];... node.primaryAxisAlignItems=main; node.counterAxisAlignItems=cross; node.primaryAxisSizingMode=mainSize; node.counterAxisSizingMode=crossSize; if(wrap) node.layoutWrap='WRAP'; return node;}\n```\n\nFrame maker:\n```js\nfunction frame(name){ const f=figma.createFrame(); f.name=name; f.fills=[]; return f; }\n```\nNote: createFrame must be appended to page before/after config; fine.\n\nAsset instance helper:\n```js\nconst comps={};\nasync function comp(id){ if(!comps[id]) comps[id]=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id); return comps[id]; }\nasync function inst(id, w, h){ const c=await comp(id); const i=c.createInstance(); if(w&&h) i.resize(w,h); else if(w){ const r=c.height/c.width... }\n```\nFor images I want fill aspect ratio preserved with FILL scaleMode — resizing instance keeps image fill. Good.\n\nIcon recolor helper:\n```js\nfunction recolor(node, hexColor){ if('fills' in node && Array.isArray(node.fills) && node.fills.length && node.fills[0].type==='SOLID'){ node.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:hexColor}]; } if('children' in node) node.children.forEach(c=>recolor(c,hexColor)); }\n```\nCareful with stars (yellow) — don't recolor those.\n\nIcon placement helper:\n```js\nasync function icon(id, size, colorHex){ const i=(await comp(id)).createInstance(); i.resize(size, size*(c.height/c.width))... \n```\nIcons have different aspect (Cart 28x28, Cart_Close 17x19...). I'll do resizeKeepRatio: i.rescale? There's rescale? For simplicity: compute scale = size/max(w,h); i.rescale(scale). Instance has rescale method (scales around origin, adjusts constraints). Yes `rescale` exists on nodes? It exists for InstanceNode? rescale is on LayoutMixin — yes.\n\nComponents must be appended to page before instances created? createInstance() then append instance to parent. Component location on page: append component to WS page at negative x coordinates.\n\nHeader build:\n\n```js\nfunction buildHeader() { const h=figma.createComponent(); h.name='F/Header'; h.resize(1440,100); h.fills=[solid white]; al(h,{mode:'HORIZONTAL', main:'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross:'CENTER', pad:[0,100,0,100]});\n // left\n const left=frame('Brand'); al(left,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:8,cross:'CENTER'}); \n const logo=inst(LogoFurniro, 48,48); left.appendChild(logo); left.appendChild(txt('Furniro',34,F.bold,'000000'));\n // nav\n const nav=frame('Nav'); al(nav,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:75,cross:'CENTER'});\n for items: t=txt(name,16,F.med,'000000'); t.name='Nav/'+name;\n // actions\n const act=frame('Actions'); al(act,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:45,cross:'CENTER'});\n icons: account 28, search 28, heart 28, cart 28.\n h.appendChild left, nav, act.\n}\n```\nComponent children appended after creation. Need to append component to page: WS.appendChild(h); h.x=-3000; h.y=0;\n\nFooter build similarly with 'F/Footer'.\n\nAlso add a 'Blog' link in Links column.\n\nPositions: keep components at x=-2000 with stacking y. I'll track compY.\n\nReturn: ids of header/footer components.\n\nAlso loadFonts upfront for all used styles.\n\nLet me now also decide text style for nav current: gold semibold + underline? I'll make current = Bold gold with small gold underline bar? Overrides per instance: color+weight is fine; underline bar needs extra node — skip bar, use weight+color. Actually to make \"current\" state clearer, I'll use gold color + SemiBold + a 2px gold underline? Without underline node in component, can't easily add per-instance. Alternative: keep it simple: current item colored gold + semibold. That's a clear state.\n\nHmm, actually I could design header nav item as a mini auto-layout (text + indicator bar hidden) but overriding visibility per instance is allowed (instance children visibility override). Simpler: color+weight. Fine.\n\nLet me write call 1 now. Also include building of \"F/FeatureStrip\" and \"F/PageTitle\"? Feature strip uses icons Trophy/Guarantee/Shipping/Support 60x60. PageTitle uses banner image 1440x316ish + logo 77 + title 48 medium + breadcrumb. I'll include both in call 1 to save round trips.\n\nPageTitle component ('F/PageBanner'): frame 1440x320: banner image instance resized 1440x320? Source 180x240 portrait... FILL crop will zoom a lot. It's a blurred room photo in original. Crop acceptable (\"Photos can be cropped freely\"). Then overlay V-AL centered: Logo_Furniro 77x77 (original uses logo 77x77 with opacity?), title 48 Medium, breadcrumb row: \"Home\" 16 medium + chevron right 20 + \"Shop\" 16 light. Title & breadcrumb as children with instance overrides per screen (override text + breadcrumb current). Wait — per screen the title differs; put texts inside, override per instance.\n\nStructure: F/PageBanner: frame 1440x320, fills banner image (use fill of the component? simpler: append instance as background child, absolute positioned, then content AL on top). Easier: set the frame's fills to the image? The image fill belongs to the component node — I can copy fills from component: f.fills = bannerComp.fills (image fill transfers!). Image fills reference imageHash — copying fill objects across nodes works. So: f.fills = (await comp('13:16')).fills → image. Nice trick, avoids instance. scaleMode FILL already.\n\nThen center content: f as AL V-AL centered gap... use primaryAxisAlignItems 'CENTER', counterAxisAlignItems 'CENTER', padding 0; content frame V-AL gap... Actually just make f itself the container: al(f,{mode:'VERTICAL', main:'CENTER', cross:'CENTER', gap:??}). Children: logo (40? original logo on banner ~ 50x77?). Media logo 13:3 is 72x72 (with inner padding?). It's 72x72 component. Use 56x56. Then title 48 Medium, then breadcrumb H-AL gap 6: Home(16 Medium black) + Icon_Chevron_Right 20 + current(16 Light).\n\nF/FeatureStrip: frame 1440x270 bg cream FCF8F3, H-AL padding [100,55,100,55], SPACE_BETWEEN, 4 items H-AL gap 10: icon 60 + V-AL gap 2: title 25 semibold dark, line 20 medium muted.\n\nIcon sizes vary (Trophy 60x60 etc). Fine.\n\nCall 1 returns component IDs. Let me write it.\n\nOne concern: figma.createComponent() + text children need fonts loaded before setting characters. txt() loads font per call — many awaits, fine.\n\nLet me write it compactly but complete.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4169e7d1-fa58-4180-9c80-2a57d8444911","uuid":"2b0ad44c-ed1b-41f7-bf2a-601579aced67","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:18:03.989Z","thinking_duration_ms":111672}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":38606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"04036ae78ff40a7a6ce54e8c143cc117","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_8_d6b92f64","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"rIFGqUvnX6ESyVMuSLCCFc","code":"\nconst WS = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('15:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(WS);\nconst hex = h => { const n=parseInt(h,16); return {r:((n>>16)&255)/255, g:((n>>8)&255)/255, b:(n&255)/255}; };\nconst sol = h => ({type:'SOLID', color:hex(h)});\nconst C = {gold:'B88E2F', ink:'000000', text:'3A3A3A', muted:'9F9F9F', soft:'666666', cream:'FCF8F3', light:'F4F5F7', banner:'F9F1E7', border:'D9D9D9', line:'EAEAEA', white:'FFFFFF', red:'E97171', green:'2EC1AC', yellow:'FFC700', dim:'1F1F1F'};\nconst F = {reg:{family:'Poppins',style:'Regular'}, med:{family:'Poppins',style:'Medium'}, sb:{family:'Poppins',style:'SemiBold'}, bold:{family:'Poppins',style:'Bold'}, light:{family:'Poppins',style:'Light'}};\nfor (const f of Object.values(F)) await figma.loadFontAsync(f);\nfunction txt(str,size,font,colorHex,opts={}){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName=font; t.fontSize=size; t.characters=str; t.fills=[sol(colorHex)]; if(opts.lh) t.lineHeight={unit:'PERCENT',value:opts.lh}; if(opts.align) t.textAlignHorizontal=opts.align; if(opts.w){ t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(opts.w, t.height);} if(opts.name) t.name=opts.name; return t; }\nfunction fr(name){ const f=figma.createFrame(); f.name=name; f.fills=[]; return f; }\nfunction al(n,o={}){ n.layoutMode=o.mode||'VERTICAL'; n.itemSpacing=o.gap||0; const p=o.pad||[0,0,0,0]; n.paddingTop=p[0]; n.paddingRight=p[1]; n.paddingBottom=p[2]; n.paddingLeft=p[3]; if(o.wrap) n.layoutWrap='WRAP'; n.primaryAxisAlignItems=o.main||'MIN'; n.counterAxisAlignItems=o.cross||'MIN'; n.primaryAxisSizingMode=o.mainSize||'AUTO'; n.counterAxisSizingMode=o.crossSize||'AUTO'; return n; }\nconst comps={};\nasync function comp(id){ if(!comps[id]) comps[id]=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id); return comps[id]; }\nasync function inst(id,w,h){ const c=await comp(id); const i=c.createInstance(); if(w&&h) i.resize(w,h); else if(w){ i.resize(w, w*c.height/c.width);} return i; }\nasync function icon(id,size,colorHex){ const c=await comp(id); const i=c.createInstance(); const s=size/Math.max(c.width,c.height); i.rescale(s); if(colorHex){ const rec=n=>{ if('fills' in n && Array.isArray(n.fills) && n.fills.some(f=>f.type==='SOLID')) n.fills=[sol(colorHex)]; if('children' in n) n.children.forEach(rec); }; rec(i);} return i; }\nlet compY = 0;\nfunction park(n){ WS.appendChild(n); n.x=-2400; n.y=compY; compY+=n.height+120; }\n\n// ---------- Header ----------\nconst LogoF='13:3', IcAcc='13:33', IcSearch='13:40', IcHeart='13:53', IcCart='13:26';\nconst header=figma.createComponent(); header.name='F/Header'; header.resize(1440,100); header.fills=[sol(C.white)];\nal(header,{mode:'HORIZONTAL', main:'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross:'CENTER', pad:[0,100,0,100]});\nconst brand=fr('Brand'); al(brand,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:8,cross:'CENTER'});\nbrand.appendChild(await inst(LogoF,48,48));\nbrand.appendChild(txt('Furniro',34,F.bold,C.ink,{name:'Brand name'}));\nconst nav=fr('Nav'); al(nav,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:75,cross:'CENTER'});\nfor(const n of ['Home','Shop','About','Contact']) nav.appendChild(txt(n,16,F.med,C.ink,{name:'Nav/'+n}));\nconst act=fr('Actions'); al(act,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:45,cross:'CENTER'});\nact.appendChild(await icon(IcAcc,28,C.ink)); act.appendChild(await icon(IcSearch,28,C.ink)); act.appendChild(await icon(IcHeart,28,C.ink)); act.appendChild(await icon(IcCart,28,C.ink));\nact.children[0].name='Account'; act.children[1].name='Search'; act.children[2].name='Wishlist'; act.children[3].name='Cart';\nheader.appendChild(brand); header.appendChild(nav); header.appendChild(act);\npark(header);\n\n// ---------- Page banner ----------\nconst banner=figma.createComponent(); banner.name='F/PageBanner'; banner.resize(1440,320);\nconst bComp=await comp('13:16'); banner.fills=JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(bComp.fills));\nal(banner,{mode:'VERTICAL', main:'CENTER', cross:'CENTER', gap:1});\nconst bLogo=await inst(LogoF,56,56); banner.appendChild(bLogo);\nconst bTitle=txt('Shop',48,F.med,C.ink,{name:'Title'}); banner.appendChild(bTitle);\nconst crumb=fr('Breadcrumb'); al(crumb,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:6,cross:'CENTER'});\ncrumb.appendChild(txt('Home',16,F.med,C.ink,{name:'Crumb root'}));\ncrumb.appendChild(await icon('13:46',20,C.ink));\ncrumb.appendChild(txt('Shop',16,F.light,C.ink,{name:'Crumb current'}));\nbanner.appendChild(crumb); park(banner);\n\n// ---------- Feature strip ----------\nconst strip=figma.createComponent(); strip.name='F/FeatureStrip'; strip.resize(1440,270); strip.fills=[sol(C.cream)];\nal(strip,{mode:'HORIZONTAL', main:'SPACE_BETWEEN', cross:'CENTER', pad:[0,55,0,55]});\nconst feats=[['13:38','High Quality','crafted from top materials'],['13:42','Warranty Protection','Over 2 years'],['13:25','Free Shipping','Order over Rs. 150,000'],['13:41','24 / 7 Support','Dedicated support']];\nfor(const [ic,t1,t2] of feats){ const item=fr('Feature'); al(item,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:10,cross:'CENTER'}); item.appendChild(await icon(ic,60,'242424')); const col=fr('Texts'); al(col,{mode:'VERTICAL',gap:2}); col.appendChild(txt(t1,25,F.sb,'242424')); col.appendChild(txt(t2,20,F.med,C.muted)); item.appendChild(col); strip.appendChild(item); }\npark(strip);\n\n// ---------- Footer ----------\nconst footer=figma.createComponent(); footer.name='F/Footer'; footer.resize(1440,505); footer.fills=[sol(C.white)];\nal(footer,{mode:'VERTICAL', gap:0});\nconst main=fr('FooterMain'); main.layoutAlign='STRETCH'; al(main,{mode:'HORIZONTAL', main:'SPACE_BETWEEN', pad:[48,100,48,100]});\nconst col1=fr('BrandCol'); al(col1,{mode:'VERTICAL',gap:50}); col1.appendChild(txt('Furniro.',24,F.bold,C.ink)); col1.appendChild(txt('400 University Drive Suite 200, Coral Gables, FL 33134 USA',16,F.reg,C.muted,{w:285,lh:150}));\nconst mkCol=(title,items)=>{ const col=fr(title); al(col,{mode:'VERTICAL',gap:46}); col.appendChild(txt(title,16,F.med,C.muted,{name:'Col title'})); for(const it of items) col.appendChild(txt(it,16,F.med,C.ink,{name:'Link/'+it})); return col; };\nconst col2=mkCol('Links',['Home','Shop','About','Contact','Blog']);\nconst col3=mkCol('Help',['Payment Options','Returns','Privacy Policies']);\nconst col4=fr('Newsletter'); al(col4,{mode:'VERTICAL',gap:46}); col4.appendChild(txt('Newsletter',16,F.med,C.muted,{name:'Col title'}));\nconst subRow=fr('SubscribeRow'); al(subRow,{mode:'HORIZONTAL',gap:11,cross:'CENTER'});\nconst inWrap=fr('EmailInput'); al(inWrap,{mode:'VERTICAL',gap:4}); const ph=txt('Enter Your Email Address',14,F.reg,C.muted); inWrap.appendChild(ph); const ul=figma.createRectangle(); ul.resize(200,1); ul.fills=[sol(C.ink)]; inWrap.appendChild(ul);\nconst subWrap=fr('SubscribeBtn'); al(subWrap,{mode:'VERTICAL',gap:4}); subWrap.appendChild(txt('SUBSCRIBE',14,F.med,C.ink,{name:'SUBSCRIBE'})); const ul2=figma.createRectangle(); ul2.resize(75,1); ul2.fills=[sol(C.ink)]; subWrap.appendChild(ul2);\nsubRow.appendChild(inWrap); subRow.appendChild(subWrap); col4.appendChild(subRow);\nmain.appendChild(col1); main.appendChild(col2); main.appendChild(col3); main.appendChild(col4);\nconst div=figma.createRectangle(); div.name='Divider'; div.layoutAlign='STRETCH'; div.resize(100,1); div.fills=[sol(C.border)];\nconst bottom=fr('FooterBottom'); bottom.layoutAlign='STRETCH'; al(bottom,{mode:'HORIZONTAL', pad:[35,100,38,100]}); bottom.appendChild(txt('2023 Furniro. All rights reserved',16,F.reg,C.ink));\nfooter.appendChild(main); footer.appendChild(div); footer.appendChild(bottom);\npark(footer);\nreturn {header:header.id, banner:banner.id, strip:strip.id, footer:footer.id, compY};\n","description":"Create core builder helpers and build Header, PageBanner, FeatureStrip and Footer components on workspace page"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4169e7d1-fa58-4180-9c80-2a57d8444911","uuid":"dd5ee866-5941-44b2-83a0-9a09be1c34b6","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:18:32.040Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_8_d6b92f64","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
