{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":114055,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081b6ae794b40a7a216c7964a5737f5a","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Something is off with absoluteTransform of instance-internal nodes in this environment — it's returning stale/weird values (x=0, y=screen bottom). The underline positions end up at bottom of frames. For screens whose header is an INSTANCE child of an auto-layout top-level frame, the absolute transform query seems broken (returns content extents?).\n\nAlternative approach: don't compute from absoluteTransform. Compute from geometry: the header instance is the first child of the screen at y=0, height 100 (after fix), full width 1440. Inside header: auto-layout with padding L/R 100, space-between. Brand width, nav width, actions width are measurable from the COMPONENT (18:2), where transforms work. Item positions relative to nav are stable (item.x relative nav).\n\nSo: navX_in_header = 1440 - 100 - actionsWidth - navWidth? No — space-between: brand at 100, actions right at 1340-actionsW, nav centered in remaining? With SPACE_BETWEEN and 3 children: brand left (x=100), actions right (x=1340-actionsW), nav in middle: remaining space distributed... With SPACE_BETWEEN, children are at edges with equal gaps between: gap = (1440 - 200 - brandW - navW - actionsW)/2. So navX = 100 + brandW + gap.\n\nunderline.x = navX + item.x (item.x relative to nav), underline.y = headerY_in_screen + nav.y + item.height + 4.\n\nFor drawer screen it computed right (header directly in fixed frame at 0,0... it gave 595.5,66 — wait it gave x=595.5 y=66, plausible!). For auto-layout parented screens it fails. Whatever — compute manually.\n\nAlso earlier underline creation (before header resize) used absoluteTransform too — those first ones were at wrong y too. Just recompute manually now.\n\nbrand width: measure component brand. nav width: measure nav. actions width: measure. item.x measured. headerY=0 always (first child, y=0).\n\ngap = (1440 - 200 - brandW - navW - actW)/2\nnavX = 100 + brandW + gap\n\nLet me do it.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4169e7d1-fa58-4180-9c80-2a57d8444911","uuid":"bbe05606-0499-4450-875b-70700a3f1d84","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:36:35.786Z","thinking_duration_ms":11005}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":114055,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081b6ae794b40a7a216c7964a5737f5a","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_55_4c66cb66","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"rIFGqUvnX6ESyVMuSLCCFc","code":"\nconst headerComp=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('18:2');\nconst brand=headerComp.findOne(n=>n.name==='Brand');\nconst navC=headerComp.findOne(n=>n.name==='Nav');\nconst actC=headerComp.findOne(n=>n.name==='Actions');\nconst gap=(1440-200-brand.width-navC.width-actC.width)/2;\nconst navX=100+brand.width+gap;\nconst navY=navC.y;\nconst SCREENS=[{id:'22:16',cur:'Home'},{id:'23:66',cur:'Shop'},{id:'24:157',cur:'Shop'},{id:'24:389',cur:'Shop'},{id:'25:553',cur:'Contact'}];\nconst gold={type:'SOLID',color:{r:0.722,g:0.557,b:0.184}};\nconst res=[];\nfor(const s of SCREENS){\n  const scr=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(s.id);\n  scr.findAll(n=>n.name==='Current nav underline').forEach(o=>o.remove());\n  const header=scr.findOne(n=>n.name==='F/Header');\n  const nav=header.findOne(n=>n.name==='Nav');\n  const item=nav.children.find(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.characters===s.cur);\n  const under=figma.createRectangle(); under.name='Current nav underline';\n  under.resize(item.width,2);\n  under.x=header.x+navX+item.x;\n  under.y=header.y+navY+item.y+item.height+4;\n  under.fills=[gold];\n  scr.appendChild(under);\n  res.push({scr:s.id,x:under.x,y:under.y});\n}\nreturn res;\n","description":"Position nav underlines via manual geometry computation from component measurements"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4169e7d1-fa58-4180-9c80-2a57d8444911","uuid":"20eebfce-b9be-4f90-a048-d59491b45a7c","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:36:39.304Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_55_4c66cb66","display_